>  
>
>> I am a bit confused by how the position of the ca'o changes its scope and 
>> effect. Does ".i la .erik. pu farlu ri'a lo bolci be lo rokci vau ca lo nu 
>> ra ca'o klama" mean that only the going is continuous?
>>
>
> It means that Eric falls at a time when the going is going on (i.e. afer 
> it started and before it is finished).  "ca'o" indicates that the event is 
> in the midst of happening (already started and not yet finished), not so 
> much that it is continuous.
>  
>
>> Also, is the use of vau correct and necessary here?
>>
>
> No, "vau" terminates the bridi, so you can't add a new term "ca lo nu ra 
> ca'o klama" after it.
>
OK. So either
.i la .erik. pu farlu ri'a lo bolci be lo rokci ca lo nu ra ca'o klama
or
.i la .erik. pu farlu ri'a lo bolci be lo rokci .i ca bo ra ca'o klama
? 

ki'e mu'o

